  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(78pt, 331.56pt, "Abstract ")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(78pt, 359.28pt, "Aromatic seed waste (ASW) has high valorisation potential due to their rich composition. ")
  #line-at(78pt, 380.04pt, "Biorefineries can optimize ASW by extracting valuable aromatic compounds through ")
  #line-at(78pt, 400.68pt, "pyrolysis and gasification, reducing waste and promoting sustainability. This study ")
  #line-at(78pt, 421.44pt, "explores the thermal valorisation of 16 different aromatic seed residues, assessing their ")
  #line-at(78pt, 442.08pt, "potential as a solid fuel and in pyrolysis.  Characterization following ISO 18122 standards ")
  #line-at(78pt, 462.84pt, "showed a moisture content below 10% (w/w), while ash content varied between 3.13% and ")
  #line-at(78pt, 483.48pt, "18.80% (w/w), exceeding normative limits in some cases. The higher heating value (HHV) ")
  #line-at(78pt, 504.24pt, "ranged from 13.55 to 20.31 MJ/kg, similar to woody and other herbaceous biomass, with ")
  #line-at(78pt, 524.88pt, "higher-density benefits for handling and storage. Thermogravimetric analysis (TGA) ")
  #line-at(78pt, 545.64pt, "identified two main degradation stages: 30–250°C, linked to simple carbohydrate ")
  #line-at(78pt, 566.28pt, "decomposition, and 250–500°C, associated with lignocellulose breakdown. These ")
  #line-at(78pt, 587.04pt, "variations impact combustion and pyrolysis performance. Elemental analysis revealed an ")
  #line-at(78pt, 607.68pt, "H/C ratio between 1.58 and 1.90, when this is greater than 1.7, it indicates better heating ")
  #line-at(78pt, 628.44pt, "value in combustion processes and better bio-oil quality in pyrolysis processes. Volatile ")
  #line-at(78pt, 649.08pt, "content of about 70% (w/w),")
  #line-at(218.16pt, 649.08pt, "these results show a sufficiently high volatile matter content, ")
  #line-at(78pt, 669.84pt, "similar to that of other biomasses, which would improve ignition at low temperatures, ")
  #line-at(78pt, 690.48pt, "making combustion more efficient.  This property favours bio-oil production, yielding a ")
  #line-at(78pt, 711.24pt, "product rich in aromatics. The results highlight ASW’s potential as a renewable energy ")
  #line-at(78pt, 731.88pt, "source and its suitability for thermal conversion processes. ")
]

