  #line-at(78pt, 119.88pt, "1. Introduction ")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(78pt, 147.6pt, "The growing demand for natural, sustainable ingredients in the nutraceutical and cosmetic ")
  #line-at(78pt, 168.36pt, "sectors has contributed to a notable increase in the cultivation of aromatic plants. In Europe, ")
  #line-at(78pt, 189pt, "the area dedicated to aromatic crops has now exceeded 100,000 hectares, with Spain alone ")
  #line-at(78pt, 209.76pt, "reporting a 35% increase in recent years, reaching approximately 18,000 hectares. The ")
  #line-at(78pt, 230.4pt, "inclusion of citrus crops used for essential oils results in a significant increase in the total ")
  #line-at(78pt, 251.16pt, "area under cultivation, which rises to approximately 72,000 hectares [1-3]. ")
  #line-at(78pt, 285.84pt, "The global market for botanical products, in which Active Medicinal Plants (AMPs) play ")
  #line-at(78pt, 306.48pt, "a major role, was valued at USD 144.38 billion in 2020 and is expected to grow at a ")
  #line-at(78pt, 327.24pt, "Compound Annual Growth Rate (CAGR) of 6.9% during the 2021–2028 period [2]. This ")
  #line-at(78pt, 347.88pt, "expansion process invariably leads to the generation of substantial quantities of by-")
  #line-at(78pt, 368.64pt, "products and residues, which typically arise as a consequence of essential oil extraction. ")
  #line-at(78pt, 389.28pt, "These residues, which are frequently underutilised, represent a potential feedstock for ")
  #line-at(78pt, 410.04pt, "bioenergy production and contribute to the closure of material loops in accordance with the ")
  #line-at(78pt, 430.68pt, "principles of the circular economy. ")
  #line-at(78pt, 465.36pt, "The circular economy model places emphasis on the valorisation of waste through ")
  #line-at(78pt, 486.12pt, "sustainable processes that generate both economic and environmental benefits. Aromatic ")
  #line-at(78pt, 506.76pt, "plant residues offer a promising opportunity for integration into biorefinery systems. The ")
  #line-at(78pt, 527.52pt, "thermochemical conversion of these materials into solid fuels, biochar, or other value-")
  #line-at(78pt, 548.16pt, "added products has been explored as an alternative to traditional disposal methods [4]. The ")
  #line-at(78pt, 568.92pt, "versatility of these residues allows for their transformation into biofuels, biochemicals, and ")
  #line-at(78pt, 589.56pt, "specialty polymers, thereby reinforcing the shift towards renewable and decentralised ")
  #line-at(78pt, 610.32pt, "energy systems. ")
  #line-at(78pt, 645pt, "Several studies have been conducted on valorisation strategies for aromatic plant residues. ")
  #line-at(78pt, 665.76pt, "Marín-Valencia et al. [5] evaluated a biorefinery model based on ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(424.32pt, 665.76pt, "Thymus vulgaris")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(507.24pt, 665.76pt, ", ")
  #line-at(78pt, 686.4pt, "combining the extraction of phenolic compounds with anaerobic digestion. While the ")
  #line-at(78pt, 707.04pt, "standalone extraction process proved more economically viable at smaller scales (23 ")
  #line-at(78pt, 727.8pt, "T/day), the biorefinery model achieved higher resource efficiency and sustainability, ")
  #line-at(78pt, 748.44pt, "despite increased energy demands. In a similar manner, Saha et al. [6] investigated ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(473.64pt, 748.44pt, "Mentha ")
]

