#original-page(595.32pt, 841.92pt, none)[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(504.48pt, 794.28pt, "4 ")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(78pt, 82.08pt, "circular resource management has been demonstrated to enhance both sustainability and ")
  #line-at(78pt, 102.72pt, "energy security. ")
  #line-at(78pt, 137.4pt, "Despite these efforts, systematic comparative studies of aromatic seed residues remain ")
  #line-at(78pt, 158.16pt, "limited. In the context of bioenergy studies, seeds are frequently overlooked despite their ")
  #line-at(78pt, 178.8pt, "potential benefits for combustion and pyrolysis due to their chemical and thermal ")
  #line-at(78pt, 199.56pt, "properties. Furthermore, there is a paucity of analyses that combine multiple species under ")
  #line-at(78pt, 220.2pt, "standardised conditions with statistical classification to guide their optimal energy use. ")
  #line-at(78pt, 255pt, "This study aims to fill this gap by evaluating the thermochemical potential of 16 aromatic ")
  #line-at(78pt, 275.64pt, "seed residues using TGA, FTIR spectroscopy, and multivariate statistical analysis. The ")
  #line-at(78pt, 296.4pt, "characterisation of the biomass samples was conducted in accordance with ISO standards, ")
  #line-at(78pt, 317.04pt, "with the objective of evaluating their suitability for utilisation as solid biofuels. The ")
  #line-at(78pt, 337.8pt, "application of statistical clustering was utilised for the identification of groups of species ")
  #line-at(78pt, 358.44pt, "that exhibited similar properties and potential applications. This approach contributed to ")
  #line-at(78pt, 379.08pt, "the more efficient and sustainable utilisation of agro-industrial residues within a circular ")
  #line-at(78pt, 399.84pt, "economy framework. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(78pt, 434.52pt, "2. Material and methods ")
  #line-at(78pt, 463.2pt, "2.1. Samples ")
