#original-page(595.32pt, 841.92pt, (image("graphics/page-17.png", width: 432.5pt), 78pt, 376pt))[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(498.6pt, 794.28pt, "17 ")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(78pt, 96.24pt, "Conversely, species with high ash/low HHV or high nitrogen—such as Sedum sediforme, ")
  #line-at(78pt, 116.88pt, "Anthemis arvensis, Thymus longiflorus, Lavandula stoechas luisieri, Mentha rotundifolia, ")
  #line-at(78pt, 137.64pt, "and Ocimum basilicum—should be avoided or limited due to their lower energy ")
  #line-at(78pt, 158.28pt, "performance and higher potential for NOx/SO₂ emissions. Operationally, maintaining a ")
  #line-at(78pt, 179.04pt, "moisture content of 6–8%, particle size between 120–200 μm, and firm compaction ")
  #line-at(78pt, 199.68pt, "improves pellet durability (Kt/Kf) and promotes more stable combustion [56,57]. ")
  #line-at(78pt, 234.36pt, "To complement the analysis carried out from the spectral data, a new principal component ")
  #line-at(78pt, 255.12pt, "analysis was performed based on the physicochemical characteristics. This approach ")
  #line-at(78pt, 275.76pt, "allows for a more complete classification of the samples and improves their discrimination ")
  #line-at(78pt, 296.52pt, "capacity. Both classifications are complementary: the PCA highlights general spectral ")
  #line-at(78pt, 317.16pt, "differences (aromatic compounds vs. waxes), while the subsequent clustering refines the ")
  #line-at(78pt, 337.92pt, "groups according to quantified chemical and energetic parameters, which are directly ")
  #line-at(78pt, 358.56pt, "linked to the quality classification of biofuels under the UNE-EN ISO 17225-6 and UNE-")
  #line-at(78pt, 379.32pt, "EN ISO 17225-7 standards. A principal component analysis was performed on the above ")
  #line-at(78pt, 399.96pt, "results. The variables considered for the analysis are moisture(%), HHV(MJ/kg), C(%), ")
  #line-at(78pt, 420.72pt, "N(%), H(%), ash(%), S(%) and volatile matter(%). Variables calculated as O(%) or FC(%) ")
  #line-at(78pt, 441.36pt, "are not included in the component analysis study because of their dependence on other ")
  #line-at(78pt, 462.12pt, "variables included in the principal component analysis. The variables estimated for the ")
  #line-at(78pt, 482.76pt, "analysis were confirmed by the Kaiser-Meyer-Olkin (KMO) test and the adequacy of the ")
  #line-at(78pt, 503.52pt, "principal component analysis by Bartett's test of sphericity. The KMO test showed a ")
  #line-at(78pt, 524.16pt, "measure of 0.612, indicating the adequacy of the sampling and the significance level ")
  #line-at(78pt, 544.92pt, "achieved in the sphericity test p<0.001 justified the use of principal component analysis.")
]

