  #line-at(78pt, 413.52pt, "estimated data. The first component, which explains 42.8% of the variance of the data ")
  #line-at(78pt, 434.16pt, "(Table 3) is positively dependent on the variables HHV (0.958), C (0.893), H (0.851), ")
  #line-at(78pt, 454.92pt, "volatile matter (0.525), and negatively on ash (-0.693), explaining the chemical and ")
  #line-at(78pt, 475.56pt, "energetic characteristics, and therefore, the quality of the different species contemplated in ")
  #line-at(78pt, 496.32pt, "the study for their use as biofuels. The second component, which explains 19.6% of the ")
  #line-at(78pt, 516.96pt, "variance of the data, is positively dependent on the variables N (0.715), S (0.865), allowing ")
  #line-at(78pt, 537.72pt, "the selection of the species that during combustion emit a greater quantity of gases that ")
  #line-at(78pt, 558.36pt, "cause, among other things, the greenhouse effect. The third component explains 17.2% of ")
  #line-at(78pt, 579.12pt, "the variance and depends positively on moisture (0.851) and ash (0.494). Like component ")
  #line-at(78pt, 599.76pt, "2, component 3 highlights negative characteristics for the use of species as biofuels. ")
]

